    "title": "Siouxland United FC clinches NPSL North Conference regular season title with 2-0 road win over Minnesota Blizzard - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Anthony Mitchell No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nSAINT PAUL, Minn. (KCAU) – The Siouxland United Outlaws secured the National Premier Soccer League (NPSL) North Conference regular season title with a 2-0 win at Minnesota Blizzard FC.\nThe win gives the Outlaws its first regular season conference championship in club history.\nSiouxland United improves to 7-0-3 while earning home field advantage for the North Conference playoffs, beginning on July 8th with the conference finals scheduled for July 11th.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KCAU 9 News | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
    "summary": "By Anthony Mitchell No media credit provided. , SAINT PAUL, Minn. (KCAU) – The Siouxland United Outlaws secured the National Premier Soccer League (NPSL) North Conference regular season title with a 2-0 win at Minnesota Blizzard FC. The win gives the Outlaws its first regular season conference championship in club history. Siouxland United improves to 7-0-3 while earning home field advantage for the North Conference playoffs, beginning on July 8th with the conference finals scheduled for July 11th. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
